\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.0.1}{\ignorespaces The running tree $T$ with the \emph  {budgeted knapsack} overlay, $V=3$. The triple below each node lists $\mathit  {dp}[v][1],\mathit  {dp}[v][2],\mathit  {dp}[v][3]$ (top-$j$ label sums in $\text  {subtree}(v)$; a leaf shows only $\mathit  {dp}[\cdot ][1]$, a $2$-node subtree only up to $[\cdot ][2]$). Sanity: root $\mathit  {dp}[1][3]=27=10{+}9{+}8$, the three largest labels; the merge of $\mathit  {dp}[2][\cdot ]$ and $\mathit  {dp}[3][\cdot ]$ into $\mathit  {dp}[1][\cdot ]$ is the child-merge \S  \ref {sec:c27-knapsack} bounds at $\ensuremath  {O(nV)}$.}}{838}{figure.caption.141}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c27-runtree-knap}{{14.0.1}{838}{The running tree $T$ with the \emph {budgeted knapsack} overlay, $V=3$. The triple below each node lists $\mathit {dp}[v][1],\mathit {dp}[v][2],\mathit {dp}[v][3]$ (top-$j$ label sums in $\text {subtree}(v)$; a leaf shows only $\mathit {dp}[\cdot ][1]$, a $2$-node subtree only up to $[\cdot ][2]$). Sanity: root $\mathit {dp}[1][3]=27=10{+}9{+}8$, the three largest labels; the merge of $\mathit {dp}[2][\cdot ]$ and $\mathit {dp}[3][\cdot ]$ into $\mathit {dp}[1][\cdot ]$ is the child-merge \secref {c27-knapsack} bounds at $\bigO {nV}$}{figure.caption.141}{}}
